\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Top:} why instructed-roleplay accuracy cannot attribute itself. The only variable such benchmarks manipulate is $E$, and no observable lies on one path but not the other. Claim truth-value $V$ and belief $B$ are distinct further parents of $S$; EXP-B (§\ref {sec:belief_strata}) varies $B$ with $E$ fixed. The fork shown is one representation among those this design cannot distinguish; the Proposition does not depend on it. \textbf  {Bottom:} what each criterion removes from reported accuracy. Only \textbf  {criterion 4}---deception varying at fixed elicitation, reachable here only on external corpora (§\ref {sec:external_audit})---can attribute what remains, and it returns a null.}}{4}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
